Subject: [PATCH] spi: airoha-snfi: report an NFI init failure

The controller probe ends in `return airoha_snand_nfi_init(priv)` with no
diagnostic, and the MTD probe loop discards the error, so a failed init shows
only as "No MTD device found". Print the error and the register base.

--- a/drivers/spi/airoha_snfi_spi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/airoha_snfi_spi.c
@@ -1073,7 +1073,13 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	return airoha_snand_nfi_init(priv);
+	ret = airoha_snand_nfi_init(priv);
+	if (ret)
+		dev_err(dev, "nfi init failed (%d); ctrl range %p, nfi range %p\n",
+			ret, regmap_get_range(priv->regmap_ctrl, 0),
+			regmap_get_range(priv->regmap_nfi, 0));
+
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int airoha_snand_nfi_set_speed(struct udevice *bus, uint speed)
